# Generated datasets, checkpoints, and experiment logs are never committed
# (CLAUDE.md: "Do not commit generated datasets, model checkpoints, or experiment logs").
# Every path here is anchored with a leading slash, which matters more than it looks.
# An unanchored `data/` matches ANY directory named data at any depth, so it silently
# swallowed `swe_sr/data/` and `tests/data/` -- hiding the entire data layer from ruff,
# which respects .gitignore. Local lint runs looked clean while checking 17 of 25 files.
# Anchored, these match only the generated output directories at the repository root.
#
# `/data/*` rather than `/data/` so the registry exception below can apply: git cannot
# re-include anything beneath an excluded directory.
/data/*
/runs/
# Slurm batch output from scripts/slurm_convmixer.sbatch. Experiment logs, so not committed;
# the numbers that matter are already in each run directory's metrics.csv and summary.json.
/logs/

# The IC registry is the one exception: it is not generated data but the immutable shared
# contract that every dataset manifest references by hash, and that both resolution pairs
# consume (D008). At ~31 KB of diffable JSON it is cheap to track, and tracking it means a
# lost registry cannot orphan a released manifest. It stays reproducible from seeds alone,
# and tests/data/test_registry.py pins its hash so a change to the sampling code is a
# visible failure rather than a silent renumbering.
!/data/registries/

# Solver demo byproducts (swe.py writes these into the working directory)
param_output.txt
*.gif
*.mp4

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.so
.Python
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# Environments
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Tooling caches
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# Editors and OS
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store

# Claude Code local overrides (agent/command definitions ARE tracked)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Rendered animations from scripts/visualize.py (large binaries, regenerable).
/viz/
